<apex:page controller="GeneratePGPMOfferLetterController"
           renderAs="pdf"
           showHeader="false"
           sidebar="false"
           applyHtmlTag="false"
           applyBodyTag="false"
           cache="false"
           contentType="application/pdf">
<html>
<head>
    <style type="text/css">
        @page {
            size: A4;
            margin: 35.5pt;
        }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            color: #000;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            font-size: 10pt;
            line-height: 1.78;
        }
        .letter-date {
            text-align: right;
            margin-bottom: 4pt;
        }
        .address-block {
            line-height: 1.78;
            margin-bottom: 20pt;
        }
        .paragraph {
            margin: 0 0 18pt 0;
            text-align: justify;
        }
        .page-break {
            page-break-before: always;
        }
        .signature-image {
            display: block;
            width: 80pt;
            height: 51pt;
            margin: 4pt 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="letter-date">{!letterDate}</div>

    <div class="address-block">
        <div>Application No: {!applicationNumber}</div>
        <div>{!applicantName}</div>
        <apex:outputPanel layout="block" rendered="{!NOT(ISBLANK(correspondenceAddressLine1))}">
            {!correspondenceAddressLine1}
        </apex:outputPanel>
        <apex:outputPanel layout="block" rendered="{!NOT(ISBLANK(correspondenceAddressLine2))}">
            {!correspondenceAddressLine2}
        </apex:outputPanel>
        <apex:outputPanel layout="block" rendered="{!NOT(ISBLANK(correspondenceAddressLine3))}">
            {!correspondenceAddressLine3}
        </apex:outputPanel>
        <apex:outputPanel layout="block" rendered="{!NOT(ISBLANK(correspondenceAddressLine4))}">
            {!correspondenceAddressLine4}
        </apex:outputPanel>
    </div>

    <p class="paragraph">Dear {!firstName},</p>

    <p class="paragraph">Congratulations!</p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        We are delighted to welcome you to S.P Jain Institute of Management &amp; Research.
        You have been selected for admission to our Post Graduate Programme in Management
        (PGPM) {!batchName}.
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        We look forward to your confirmation and acceptance of the offer of admission with
        deposit of admission fees of Rs. 65,000/- latest by {!offerDeadline}. The signed
        letter of acceptance (as detailed in Annexure 1) needs to be uploaded to the
        admission portal by {!offerDeadline}. The 1st installment of fees of Rs.10,85,000
        is payable by {!firstInstallmentDeadline} and the balance amount of Rs. 10,00,000
        needs to be paid by {!balanceFeePaymentDeadline}. All fee payments as per Annexure 2 are to be
        made through wire/NEFT/RTGS transfer.
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        Should you choose to withdraw your acceptance, the refund will be in accordance
        with the refund policy, as detailed in Annexure 3. Please refer to the offer details
        document and annexures for more information on the admission requirements.
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        The programme will commence on {!programmeStartDate}. The instructions for online
        registration will be sent to you separately. The programme will be in conformance
        with the required safety measures undertaken by the institute. SPJIMR reserves the
        right to conduct sessions/classes on an online or on-campus mode as deemed fit by
        the Institute in light of Central &amp; State Government directives to comply with
        procedures that do not endanger public health safety norms.
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        We request you to keep the following important points in mind:
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        As a participant, you should have completed 3 years of work experience on the day
        of the commencement of the programme to be eligible for the programme. If at any
        point in time, it is discovered that the above condition is not met, the Institute
        reserves the right to cancel the admission. In such an event, the refund rules as
        per the Annexure 3 will apply. Further any change in your role or current employment
        including resignation from your job, must be duly brought to the notice of the
        Admissions Office. The Institute reserves the right to re-examine your candidature
        in light of the above-mentioned changes.
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">
        This admission offer is also subject to your meeting all eligibility requirements
        including entrance test scores (CAT/GMAT) as entered in the application form being
        validated by the concerned testing authority.
    </p>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <p class="paragraph">
        Your acceptance of this Offer of Admission implies your agreement to all
        stipulations, terms &amp; conditions, etc. as conveyed through this offer letter,
        offer details and its annexures. SPJIMR reserves the right to withdraw the Offer
        of Admission at any stage if it is found that you are not meeting the eligibility
        criteria and/or have misrepresented any fact about your candidature at any point
        of time. All claims/disputes must be settled under Mumbai jurisdiction only.
    </p>

    <p class="paragraph">We look forward to you joining the SPJIMR community.</p>

    <div>Best Wishes,</div>
    <img src="{!URLFOR($Resource.PGPMOfferLetterSignature)}"
         class="signature-image"
         alt="Dr. Renuka Kamath signature" />
    <div>Dr. Renuka Kamath</div>
    <div>Associate Dean - Full Time Programmes; Professor of Marketing</div>
    <div>S.P. Jain Institute of Management and Research, Mumbai</div>
</body>
</html>
</apex:page>